      "author": "glajciorz",
      "author_id": null,
      "post_date": "Fri Oct 05, 2007 6:25 pm",
      "post_datetime": "2007-10-05T23:25:00+00:00",
      "post_subject": "Crystals (aka \"The Fall of the Fixer\")",
      "content_md": "This piece of film is 3,5x2,5cm, so it's rather small window \n\nYAGna puts out 8-15mJ of 532nm, but SSY1 I'm driving SSY1 at very low power (6,7J; starts lasing at 4,8J).\n\nI tested the laser up to 9J and it gave 36-40mJ of green.\n\nAt full power (15J) i would expect something like 50-55mJ output.\n\nLamp can be overdriven to 30J, but the original q-switch won't survive such a punishment.\n\nIf more power is needed I always have 500J in fast Maxwell caps of 4500J in electrolytics \n\ngreetings\n\nAdam",
      "signature": "",
      "attachments": [],
      "quotes": [],
      "is_first_post": false,
